factors, including required hashrates, technological changes, the availability of hardware and other inputs, and production costs. The
Company reassesses the estimated useful lives of its mining equipment when indicators suggest that the productive life of the assets
is longer or shorter than previously estimated.</span></p></ix:nonNumeric><div>

