<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">For the period from the Closing Date through June
30, 2026, amortization expense related to the co-development rights was $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdjustmentForAmortization" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-8251">118,664</ix:nonFraction>. In June 2026, the Company determined that continued
investment in development activities related to the co-development rights was not warranted at that time. This determination constituted
a triggering event under ASC 360-10-35, <i>Property, Plant, and Equipment &#8211; Subsequent Measurement</i>, requiring the Company to
test the co-development rights for recoverability. Management determined that the carrying amount of the GEAR-related rights was not fully
recoverable and estimated the fair value of the rights to be approximately $<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zsqr:EstimatedTheFairValue" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-8252">450,000</ix:nonFraction> based on the amount management expects to recover
